			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3583394">
									

<p>Okay. So.</p>
<p>My first impression was &quot;It's 579 meets 055 meets The Light That Died&quot;.</p>
<p>But I think this actually takes the concepts of all three of those articles to the next level.</p>
<p>This isn't anitmemetics, or not <em>just</em> antimemetics. It's like&#8230; an anti-concept. They don't know what's in there, and they seem incapable of understanding that they don't know this. They're just sort of going through the motions of testing and containing, without any specifics as to what's going on or why anything is happening. And what makes it work is the fact that literally no one at the Foundation (well, anyone writing this document) is questioning the lack of information.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Following insemination, Subject undergoes a macroscopic mitosis-meiosis event, resulting in a loss of biomass.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>And literally what the fuck is this.</em></p>
<p>This is subtle and devious and might even be brilliant. I'm not sure I can fully grasp what this is, or what's going on, but I am assured of the logic behind it. Fantastic.</p>

